From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: Decode VC-1 Main profile without B pictures

Main profile was refused for chroma drift across P pictures and luma
errors with FASTUVMC. The drift was the 32-byte reference pitch, fixed
by "media: cedrus: Lay VC-1 pictures out at a 32-byte pitch"; SMPTE's
SMM0015, with FASTUVMC and no B pictures, now decodes bit-exact.

B pictures still come out a little off: SMPTE's SMM0005 gives every I
and P picture bit-exact and its B pictures at 37 to 58 dB. Refuse Main
profile only where the sequence allows B pictures.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_dec_vc1.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_dec_vc1.c
@@ -821,12 +821,8 @@
 	if (slice->sequence.profile == V4L2_VC1_PROFILE_COMPLEX)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	/*
-	 * Main profile decodes incorrectly, against the SMPTE conformance
-	 * streams: chroma drifts across P pictures in a stream with B
-	 * pictures, and luma too with FASTUVMC.
-	 */
-	if (slice->sequence.profile == V4L2_VC1_PROFILE_MAIN)
+	/* Main profile's B pictures decode a little off: SMPTE's SMM0005, 37 dB */
+	if (slice->sequence.profile == V4L2_VC1_PROFILE_MAIN && slice->metadata.maxbframes)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	/* Reduced-resolution (multi-res) coding is not supported. */
